From: yuma shimizu <46545607+mouseos@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zz-native-board-launch-hook: optional board hook before launchd

With XNU_BOARD_LAUNCH=1 (CONFIG_XNU_BOARD_LAUNCH=y) load_init_program calls unixnu_board_launch(p, scratch), which
a device repository supplies in its board archive (XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES), right before the default init programs
(launchd) are executed, after the root, SystemOS and Data mounts. The scratch page is the user page load_init_program
already maps for init's arguments. A nonzero result stops the boot. Boards without the flag build the unchanged
function. The hook sits away from the hunks of the owner mount, AIR init and boot progress patches, so each of them
still reverses and applies cleanly in the incremental passes of build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -7470,6 +7470,18 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
+#if defined(XNU_BOARD_LAUNCH) && XNU_BOARD_LAUNCH
+	/*
+	 * Board hook: a device repository links an archive (XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES) that defines unixnu_board_launch().
+	 * It runs once, as init (pid 1) before launchd, with the root and the owner volumes mounted.
+	 */
+	{
+		extern int unixnu_board_launch(void *process, uint64_t scratch);
+		int board_error = unixnu_board_launch(p, (uint64_t)scratch_addr);
+		if (board_error) panic("board launch hook failed: %d", board_error);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	error = ENOENT;
 	for (i = 0; i < sizeof(init_programs) / sizeof(init_programs[0]); i++) {
 		printf("load_init_program: attempting to load %s\n", init_programs[i]);
